package react

const reasoningRequestPrompt = `Reasoning mode selection is part of this normal decision, not a separate classification request. When runtime_features includes reasoning_request, first decide from the current requested operation, relevant conversation and retained evidence whether to use the fast path or request_reasoning. Use the fast path for conversation, retrieving saved records, brief factual or qualitative explanations including side-by-side concept definitions, and executing a known calculation with complete inputs. A request limited to explaining or briefly comparing concept meanings uses the fast path, including professional terminology. Words in record titles or quotations identify the subject. For recommendations that weigh alternatives against interacting constraints, causal diagnosis, proofs, or plans requiring multi-step inference, you must select request_reasoning before drawing conclusions, even when the requested answer is short or the inputs are hypothetical. Short follow-ups inherit the actual work from the conversation. You may collect missing evidence first. If essential inputs or a callable capability are absent, ask for the essential input or explain that limitation directly; upgrading cannot supply missing capabilities or evidence. Select request_reasoning through the configured output channel with no payload, explanation or hidden reasoning. It enables deeper reasoning for subsequent normal decisions, consumes one ordinary round and token budget, and is available at most once per run. After reasoning_requested is true, continue the work without requesting another upgrade. Authorization and business approval remain enforced by the runtime.`
